(4,'KEEP',[],'theory','Cell-swallowing geometry under explicit volume and surface constraints','The liquid/dry volume proportions, minimum granule volume and maximum pseudopodium surface are supplied. Geometric packing and volume/surface optimization bound meal size; no cell membrane biochemistry or force law is requested.'),
(5,'KEEP',[I],'experimental','Lifted falling bead chain and pickup momentum/energy','Actual flexible bead-chain/glass description defines ordinary variable-mass momentum, tensions and a pickup reaction. Declared bead-contact/pickup assumptions explain a chain fountain and its energy; deriving a molecular contact material law is unnecessary.'),
(6,'BORDERLINE',[IV],'experimental','Size evolution of an effervescent tablet','Mass balance with a measured surface dissolution/reaction flux is ordinary experimental modelling. Predicting the flux and changing shape from the bare statement can instead depend centrally on unsupplied reaction/dissolution/bubble-transport kinetics. No law or measured parameters resolve that model depth.'),
(7,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','In-plane small modes of a suspended inextensible chain','Catenary gravity/tension, local Newton force balance and linearized length constraints generate variable-coefficient waves and modes. No unsupplied bending elasticity or specialized viscous fluid theory is needed.'),
(8,'KEEP',[I],'numerical','Seasonal Earth rotation estimates under changing mass distributions','Angular momentum, changing inertia and atmospheric/ocean angular momentum give ordinary estimates. Historical/future geography/climate inputs must be declared as scenarios/parameters; a unique greenhouse forecast is not established from the short statement.'),
