(10,'KEEP',[I],'theory','Unrolling a lossless variable-mass hoop with supplied target relations','The explicit hoop idealization, negligible losses/gravity and normalized speed/force formulas define a Newton momentum/energy problem. Track detached stationary hose and fixed-end angular momentum rather than applying constant-mass formulas.'),
(11,'REJECT',[],'numerical','Force to plastically fold a bottle cap approximated as a flat disk','Geometry and permission to neglect rim detail do not supply plate bending rigidity, buckling or plastic yield moment. Those central unsupplied shell/plate constitutive relations set the force; bare scalar compression is insufficient.'),
(12,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Acoustic transmission through a stipulated membrane/bone mechanical sequence','The statement permits rubber-layer and solid mechanical approximations. Ordinary wave impedance, lumped lever/inertia and layered resonance describe intensity changes under parameterized geometry/material data. Chemical hearing conversion is background, not a required biochemical derivation.'),
(13,'KEEP',[I,II],'theory','Whole swinging-Atwood elevator model under specified impulse and counterweight','All five operational questions use ordinary variable-length pendulum/Atwood constraints, Newton forces, rigid-cabin torque and rope tension. Geometry, passenger masses and strength remain explicit parameters; no specialist lift-control or material fracture theory is requested.'),
(14,'KEEP',[I,II],'numerical','Air displacement around breathing with body-volume compensation','Volume conservation and a declared low-speed source/sink geometry estimate radial displacement; body expansion cancels or modifies the leading monopole. Detection threshold and breathing scale are parameters. Exact turbulent respiratory flow is not required.'),
(15,'KEEP',[IV],'theory','Hot-water pipe thermal transients and sinusoidal tap mixing','Advection of measured flow, ordinary heat exchange/conduction and hot/cold mixing give the time dependence. The angular-flow law is supplied; wall-temperature profile and thermal coefficients can be parameters without deriving turbulent pipe resistance.'),
(16,'KEEP',[III,V],'theory','Two-dimensional foam area change from capillary pressure and scalar gas diffusion','Capillary pressure, surface-tension force balance at three-film junctions and gas diffusion through films reduce area rate to a curvature/turning-angle sum. The diffusion coefficient is given; geometric angle closure yields the side-count threshold without a full fluid transport or elastic film model.'),
