(18,'KEEP',[I,III],'theory','Constructing a hydraulic black-box model with inverse level response','The task explicitly permits choosing a simple model. Hydrostatic pressure, levers/floats/pistons and volume conservation can generate and analyze a proposed state-dependent response, with stability/passivity limitations disclosed; no unique unseen apparatus is asserted.'),
(19,'KEEP',[],'experimental','Comparing fully supplied von Mises and Tresca yield criteria','Both complete stress-eigenvalue/invariant criteria are printed. Matrix algebra compares them, and known-load stress tests can distinguish their predictions without deriving an unprovided tensor constitutive response. The literal three-dimensional trace versus two-dimensional claim must be checked.'),
(20,'BORDERLINE',[I,III,IV],'theory','Spherical cavity collapse, elastic interior collisions and driven gas-bubble extrema','An ideal spherical incompressible-flow energy model and gas thermodynamics allow substantial Newtonian analysis. Actual minimum size, collapse cutoff and driven heat response may centrally require unprovided compressibility/viscosity/interface closure. The source fixes neither ideal assumptions nor full dynamics, leaving whole-task model depth uncertain.'),
(21,'KEEP',[I,V],'experimental','Connected retained water in a supplied close-packed sphere model','The exact close-packed fixed-sphere geometry allows capillary pressure, gravity, wetting and pore-connectivity bounds. Size/contact-angle parameters and optional observation determine retention; no quantitative viscous drainage transient is requested.'),
