(23,'REJECT',[],'theory','Rotating rod lateral buckling threshold and Green-function analysis','Young modulus and linear density are given, but bending moment-curvature/flexural rigidity, cross-section and endpoint constraints are not. Those central specialized beam laws determine the instability equation before the suggested integral mathematics.'),
(24,'BORDERLINE',[IX],'experimental','One-way light-speed measurement and clock-synchronization conventions','Ordinary timing, detector delays and spatially offset clock readings give substantial experimental/convention analysis. A full proof and SR consequence can require unsupplied simultaneity/clock-transport postulates. No operational synchronization model fixes the intended depth; retain the whole conceptual boundary.'),
